{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-129032",
  "enisaUuid": "8c4ada4f-5276-3c03-9cce-4eb11a886e74",
  "description": "A vulnerability in the Ultimate Packer for eXecutables (UPX) unpacker of ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition on an affected device.\r  \r This vulnerability is due to improper length checks, when unpacking the UPX files, which may result in an out-of-bounds read of heap memory. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by submitting a crafted UPX for decode. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the ClamAV decode process to terminate, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:32:49 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:45:13 PM",
  "baseScore": 7.5,
  "baseScoreVersion": "3.1",
